berkeley-heat-pain.logic.r2: argue/equivocates: P1 (S1): "pain" is taken as has something painful, i.e. bears a quality that causes pain in a perceiver in P1 and as feels pain, as only a perceiving being can where pain is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C (S17) does not follow (berkeley-heat-pain.logic.r2.sense1)
berkeley-heat-pain.logic.r2: argue/countermodel: C (S17): D = {matter}; heat = {matter}, pain = ∅, pain_2 = {matter}
